/**
 * AuthoringService is the in-game dungeon builder's seam: write a world file,
 * get back the world the game will play.
 *
 * THIS IS THE SECOND AuthoringService AT THIS PATH, AND A REPLACEMENT, NOT A
 * REVISION (rpg-project PR #255, slice rpg-project#256). The first described
 * the room-chain dialect — `FloorPlan`, `door_row`, `start_column`, an
 * `archetype` that silently chose where the party stood — and its only server
 * was deleted with the old encounter module in rpg-api#801. Under
 * no-backcompat there is nothing to stay compatible with, so the old shapes
 * are gone rather than reserved: there is no wire to keep safe, and carrying
 * a dead dialect beside a live one is the Rule 1 violation this repo already
 * pays for once.
 *
 * The one idea that survives from the first cut is the transport decision:
 * a malformed REQUEST is a gRPC status, a file that fails to COMPILE is a
 * body. See PutDungeonRequest.
 *
 * ListDungeons, DeleteDungeon and RenameDungeon were deliberately absent
 * while nothing in the builder's loop (draw, validate, save, play, reopen)
 * listed, deleted or renamed — an RPC with no caller is the Rule 4 violation
 * this repo is still paying down elsewhere. The studio's Open panel is their
 * caller (rpg-project#585): it lists what the author can open, and renames
 * and deletes the author's own.
 *
 * TWO STORES, ONE WORLD (rpg-project#585, design R20–R24). Every dungeon RPC
 * here acts for the caller in the caller's world — the one the auth boundary
 * verified for the request, never a request field. Writes land only in that
 * world's store, each record owned by the caller's player id; the server's
 * shipped references are read-only. A key is unique within a world and
 * resolves world store first, then shipped. A request with no trusted world
 * is FailedPrecondition "trusted world context is required".
 *
 * The refusal sentences below are the status messages, verbatim: a client
 * shows them where the author is looking (the key field, the panel row), so
 * they are part of the contract.
 *
 * @generated from service dnd5e.api.authoring.v1alpha1.AuthoringService
 */
